Z||000000||Will||01-09-2001||05:31 PM||||I know it's only been posted a few dozen times, but where is the list of OEM wheels that will fit Fieros?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||stsmithgt||01-09-2001||07:01 PM||||This list?<P>Here’s a list of wheels that will fit our cars <BR>I thought all the new members we have gotten lately would like to know <P>BUICK<BR>SKYHAWK, SKYLARK, 88-UP <BR>SOMERSET <BR>CADILLAC<BR>CIMARRON 81-88 <BR>CHEVY<BR>BERETTA, CORSICA 87-97 <BR>GTU, GTZ, Z-26 89-97 <BR>CAVALIER 81-UP <BR>Z24 89-UP <BR>CELEBRITY 82-90 <BR>CITATION 80-85 <BR>X-11 81-85 <BR>MALIBU, CHEVELLE 97-UP <BR>CHRYSLER<BR>LEBARON 86-95 <BR>LASER, GTS 85-88 <BR>NEW YORKER 86-93 <BR>SEBRING CONVERTIBLE 96-UP <BR>DODGE<BR>ARIES, 400, 600 86-88 <BR>DAYTONA, TURBO Z 85-93 <BR>DYNASTY 88-93 <BR>LANCER 85-89 <BR>SHADOW 87-94 <BR>SPIRIT 89-94 <BR>STRATUS 95-UP <BR>LEXUS<BR>ES, 250 90-93 <BR>OLDSMOBILE<BR>ACHIEVA 92-97 <BR>CUTLASS CALAIS, 82-89<BR>CIERA, FIRENZA <BR>PLYMOUTH<BR>ACCLAIM 89-95 <BR>BREEZE 95-UP <BR>CARAVELLE 85-88 <BR>LASER 85-89 <BR>RS, TURBO 85-89 <BR>NEON 5-LUG 95-99 <BR>RELIANT, TOURISMO 85-89 <BR>SUNDANCE 87-94 <BR>PONTIAC<BR>6000, LE 82-90 <BR>FIERO, GT 84-88 <BR>GRANDAM 85-98<BR>SE, GT 85-98 <BR>SUNBIRD, J2000 82-94 <BR>SUNFIRE GT 95-UP <BR>TOYOTA<BR>CAMRY 86-91 <BR>CELICA 92-00 <BR>VOLKSWAGEN<BR>BEETLE 99-UP <BR>CORRADO VR6 92-93 <BR>JETTAIII (4CYL) 99-UP <BR>JETTAIII VR6 93-UP <BR>GLX VR6 92-98 <BR>GOLF 2000 <BR>That’s all folks!!!! <P>||||reg||7
Z||000002||Raydar||01-09-2001||11:07 PM||||Some of the newer Subaru wheels will fit, too. (I'm kinda partial to the Forrester wheels. 16x6.5, if I remember correctly)||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||01-10-2001||09:47 AM||||Speaking of Forester,  I was at a shop that had to replace a sparkplug wire on one of those.  Not covered by waranty either.  22+ dollars for ONE plug wire. ouch.||||reg||13
Z||000004||Raydar||01-10-2001||11:28 AM||||$22?! Jeez!<BR>I think it shoulda been covered under warranty, anyway.<BR>Aren't new cars required to carry emissions compliance warranties for 50,000 miles? Seems like a spark plug wire would qualify.<BR>IMHO.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||01-10-2001||04:08 PM||||Is there a page anywhere in which these are listed by diameter, width, and offset/backspacing?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||01-10-2001||04:12 PM||||Will,<P>Check out <A HREF="http://www.aaarims.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.aaarims.com</A>  .<P>You'll have to poke around a bit, but they list bolt circle, and sometimes offset, for most everything. Pics, too. <BR>Check the overstock section, too. Those prices are a little more reasonable. Not great, though. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||qwikgta||01-10-2001||07:22 PM||||There is a company called AIM that makes a wheel adapter that changes the bolt circle from 5X100mm to 5X4.5inch.  The adapter adds 1.25 inch to the offset.  They sell for $39.00 each.  Not sure if they have a web site but here is the number.  1-800-289-9980<P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top||||reg||6
